   "source": [
    "## Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Project Goal:** Determine the \"Best Neighborhood for Retirees\" in Pittsburgh.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Approach:** Create a composite index based on `Safety`, `Air Quality`, and `Infrastructure`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Metric Selection Process:** We established a composite index to quantify \"bestness\". After brainstorming various factors like walkability, noise pollution, and property values, we narrowed our focus to three critical, data-available pillars:\n",
    "\n",
    "1.  **Safety**: Retirees are often more vulnerable to crime, making safety a non-negotiable priority.\n",
    "\n",
    "2.  **Air Quality**: Respiratory health becomes increasingly important with age. We wanted to find areas with consistently clean air.\n",
    "\n",
    "3.  **Infrastructure**: Access to essential services (medical stations, police) and quality-of-life facilities (parks, senior centers) defines daily convenience.\n",
    "\n",
    "We rejected metrics like \\\"Number of Bars\\\" or \\\"School Ratings\\\" as they are less relevant to our target persona.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The Metric\n",
    "\n",
    "**Safety (Safety Score):**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Dataset: Monthly Criminal Activity (2024-2025), Population(2020).\n",
    "\n",
    "- Measure: Inverse of serious crime rate per capita.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Air Quality (BNAS - Best Neighborhood Air Score):**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Dataset: Daily Air Condition (2024-2025).\n",
    "\n",
    "- Measure: Composite score based on daily median AQI, P90 AQI, and healthy days ratio.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Infrastructure (Infrastructure Score):**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Dataset: City Facilities, Population(2020).\n",
    "\n",
    "- Measure: Weighted per capita density of key facilities (Police, Medic, Senior Centers, Parks, etc.).\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
